# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1
# HTTP stand-in for the Jira and Confluence Server/DC REST API an mcp-atlassian deployment points
# JIRA_URL and CONFLUENCE_URL at. Jira Software DC and Confluence DC run within the memory bound
# and set up with no person under Atlassian's published Data Center timebomb licenses, which need
# no account, but those licenses expire three hours after they are applied, which would tie every
# run to a three-hour window, so the maintainer keeps this stand-in. It answers three routes:
#   GET /rest/api/2/search?jql=...  (jira.jql, the Server/DC path)
#   GET /rest/api/2/issue/<key>     (jira.get_issue, for each key the Jira searches return)
#   GET /rest/api/search?cql=...    (confluence.cql)
# Each branches on the whole query mcp-atlassian builds (0.22.0, and 0.21.1 for the fix check)
# with JIRA_PROJECTS_FILTER=PROJ and CONFLUENCE_SPACES_FILTER=TEAM, listed below in PROJ_JQLS,
# DEMO_JQLS and CQL_RESULTS, never on a word inside it.
# Outputs: the Jira search is the response of "Searching for issues and restricting the issue
# fields returned in the results" in the Jira Data Center REST API examples
# (https://developer.atlassian.com/server/jira/platform/jira-rest-api-examples/), elision lines
# dropped, its project key QA replaced by PROJ; the Confluence search is MOCK_CQL_SEARCH_RESPONSE
# (tests/fixtures/confluence_mocks.py) of mcp-atlassian v0.22.0, copied. The DEMO project and
# space are copies of the same outputs with identifiers replaced. The issue is
# MOCK_JIRA_ISSUE_RESPONSE (tests/fixtures/jira_mocks.py) of mcp-atlassian v0.22.0, copied, the
# Jira reference giving no whole example of it: issue_detail replaces its host
# https://example.atlassian.net by the search example's http://localhost:8080, its key and id by
# those of the search's issue, and for a DEMO issue the project key PROJ by DEMO; any other key
# answers 404 with the empty ErrorCollection below. Any other JQL answers 400 with
# the ErrorCollection schema of the Jira Data Center 10.3 REST reference (errorMessages, errors),
# which gives no example value, so both are empty; any other CQL answers 400 with the RestError
# schema of the Confluence Data Center REST reference ("returned if the query cannot be parsed"),
# whose properties give no example value, so only its statusCode is set; any other method or path
# answers 404 with that empty ErrorCollection. No Server header is sent.
# DEMO_SUMMARY, when set, gives the DEMO issues of the searches a summary and replaces the title
# and excerpt of the DEMO page (a per-launch container only).
FROM python@sha256:a6e34c598f2467ed0e9a8d349809fcd8b5c603269512df273a0bb1784edc11b1

RUN cat > /responder.py <<'PY'
